he caption for smaller width?"],["41e3cdd6_89e48369",26,-7,1,"nit: prefer `Rect` or `Insets`"],["41fa5cb3_3ab49ac2",27,-7,0,"There's `UrlBar` or something like that I'd be leaning to use instead of the `TextView` since it should be designed to hold urls => be secure. Have you considered using it?"],["52b5fdb9_79c27b47",25,-7,0,"Just a sidenode - I'd check up with CCT origin update logic, because there might be some edge-cases when this method is not invoked, but an \"unrelated\" one does."],["6da2aed0_b3135dcf",25,-7,1,"nit: prefer `Context` instead."],["ca73be28_8df0dad2",26,-7,1,"nit: `IS_TITLE_VISIBLE` or `TITLE_VISIBLE`"],["0023d8d8_6f93e499",28,-2,1,"nit: maybe just `custom_tabs_popup_title_bar_min_height` and `custom_tabs_popup_title_bar_min_size`? Dimens should satisfy a11y requirements anyway, so the reason seems to be redundant."],["34264a48_37e4e07a",25,-2,0,"As a follow-up - I'd also propose to listen to `onConfigurationChanged` to recalculate `lp.height`."],["376eedbf_b17b5b53",27,-2,1,"Why is it needed? Shadows?"],["46baf08d_b86f47e7",25,-2,0,"nit: that's redundant, the doc says that update is dispatched when `AppHeaderState` changes."],["74c8bb4e_addc4137",27,-2,1,"Can we use `wrap_content`? That's just more predictable and doesn't rely on the manual measurements."],["a6140b75_9a27f3fa",29,-2,1,"nit: maybe `HEADER_PADDINGS`? It should be more future-proof if more controls are added."],["d8667c1d_fdd2bbbc",25,-2,0,"nit: the interface doesn't have `@Nulllable`, so we can assume `newState` is non-nullable."],["f68d0722_9a97512f",30,-2,0,"Let's anchor its top to the `ViewStub` bottom, e.g. `*_below=\"@+id/desktop_popup_header\"`. Also, why do we need `LinearLayout`? Can we use `FrameLayout`?"],["ab807804_297c4f32",31,-1,1,"We can probably remove the detail about the feature flag."],["afa8e2c5_9e7c5ede",27,-1,1,"@mschillaci@google.com to confirm this is correct usage of ToolbarHairlineView."],["bca98ea4_97895ea9",31,-1,1,"nit: can annotate with @LayoutRes"],["d11a333d_5bd0691d",28,-1,1,"min_touch_target_size?"],["e24382f0_1877ac9a",27,-1,1,"First time seeing `~`s used like this. Is it a common pattern?"],["f4bc1f19_e9e3f878",32,-1,1,"We can probably make this a Robolectric test."],["fa2e2929_c34e1421",31,-1,1,"nit: can annotate with @IdRes"]],0,46],[7146430,20411,52,1.144,0.818,[[15,21]],[],0,47],[7146822,20411,3,0.142,0.088,[[22,0.6,8,2],[21,0.4,4,1]],[],0,48],[7217208,20424,2,0.142,0.088,[[1,7]],[],0,49],[7221770,20428,98,2.113,1.57,[[14,0.409,16,43],[1,0.191,8,19],[9,0.183,2,19],[15,0.07,22,6],[22,0.061,9,5],[31,0.043,0,3],[0,0.026,11,2],[26,0.017,6,1]],[["51bb1d1e_2681dac3",33,-3,1,"What do you think about the approach from the previous discussions [1]? Imo, it's just more explicit that we check that feature is supported than just SDK version. [1]…"]],0,50]]}